6785	{"artifactId":"LLD-a20c9d2b51002bec-s1","entry":{"id":"review-5860aec14bb2180634801505c843b558","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:00:13.056Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Binding gate fixtures to their actual BUILD addresses the stated freshness failure without relaxing approval rules.","evidence":"The ISSUE identifies bare review fixtures. writeCR in approve-codereview-gate.test.ts writes only verdict and counts; reviewBuildGap requires subject.changedFiles and a matching subject.buildFingerprint. Both enforceCodeReviewGate and otherPartyReviewGap call that guard before accepting BUILD completion. [files: docs/standalone/fix-23-failing-tests-workflow-gate-E20261026a20c9d2b/ISSUE.md, src/workflow/__tests__/approve-codereview-gate.test.ts, src/workflow/code-review/build-freshness.ts, src/workflow/code-review/gate.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts]","action":"Implement the proposed fixture correction while retaining verdict, counts and reviewer-party variations.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Explicit default review settings eliminate the call-limits assertion's dependence on user configuration.","evidence":"The test calls reviewDeadlineMs('issue') and reviewDeadlineMs('feature') without settings. Its implementation defaults to readDesignReviewSettings(), which reads PATHS.config. DEFAULT_DESIGN_REVIEW_SETTINGS supplies 12- and 18-minute deadlines, both above the 300-second session silence limit. [files: src/workflow/review/__tests__/call-limits.test.ts, src/workflow/review/template.ts]","action":"Pass DEFAULT_DESIGN_REVIEW_SETTINGS to both deadline calls.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The installed LMDB library's lock-loss behavior justifies changing the pinned read error expectation.","evidence":"Read both reproduction cases and runLockLossSequence. The raw case expects -30775/MDB_LOCK_FAILURE; the store-backed case expects 22/MDB_BAD_RSLOT. Confirming the installed library requires executing child processes that create temporary stores, which this read-only environment does not permit. The analyzer returned an off-topic, incomplete bundle and supplied no runtime evidence. [files: src/db/graph/__tests__/lock-loss-reproduction.test.ts, src/db/graph/__tests__/helpers/store-child-driver.ts]","action":"Before changing assertions, record the observed code and message separately for raw and store-backed cases; retain transaction and healthy-control assertions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The named inventory and build-record correction sites correspond to the actual stale expectations.","evidence":"ARTIFACT_WRITE_INVENTORY lists daemon/index.ts but not handler-runtime.ts. handler-runtime.ts directly writes PATHS.config in config.write, while index.ts delegates runtime construction. The t7 test reads uppercase S001 paths; all three corresponding lowercase s1 JSON records are tracked and contain string body.commit values. [files: src/workflow/artifact-write-inventory.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/daemon/index.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/__tests__/build-record.test.ts, .insrc/artifacts/BUILD-972bf31d13c81a2f-s1.json, .insrc/artifacts/BUILD-c90f3fe60b90dd44-s1.json, .insrc/artifacts/BUILD-be8708a9cd20e286-s1.json]","action":"Update the production inventory metadata explicitly; describe handler-runtime.ts as a non-artifact config writer. Replace the three t7 paths as proposed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed fixture construction can preserve the existing freshness and file-coverage invariants.","evidence":"reviewBuildGap rejects invalid verdicts, absent or malformed changedFiles, missing or mismatched fingerprints, and uncovered changeLog target.file values. The proposed builder supplies precisely these fields. Existing helpers/other-party-review.ts already derives coverage and fingerprint this way. The prose adequately describes the BUILD-to-review binding; no changed runtime relationship or UX requires a companion visual. [files: src/workflow/code-review/build-freshness.ts, src/workflow/__tests__/helpers/other-party-review.ts, src/workflow/__tests__/other-party-review-gate.test.ts]","action":"Extract or reuse the existing helper logic, preserving caller-supplied party metadata and intentional corrupt/absent-review cases.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The acceptance mapping provides meaningful checks for restored outcomes, guard preservation and repeatability.","evidence":"The cited gate tests assert approval results and specific block or same-party reasons, so malformed fixtures cannot satisfy them merely by being withheld. Inventory checks scan production writers. convert-repeat compares interrupted runs with a reference and separately asserts byte-identical second application. The planned builder test adds rejection cases for each required field, stale binding and missing coverage; workflow/db sweeps cover ac4. These are planned checks, not verified passing results. [files: src/workflow/__tests__/approve-build-completion.test.ts, src/workflow/__tests__/approve-codereview-gate.test.ts, src/workflow/__tests__/other-party-review-gate.test.ts, src/workflow/__tests__/artifact-write-inventory.test.ts, src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-repeat.test.ts, src/workflow/__tests__/approve-build-freshness.test.ts, src/workflow/__tests__/helpers/other-party-review.ts]","action":"Keep the second-apply byte comparison unmasked. Add the builder rejection cases as specified, and record baseline versus final failure and skip counts. Share construction with the existing valid-review helper to avoid duplicate fixture logic.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":6,"unverified":1},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-26T08:00:13.056Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
